---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Services — Eight34 Labs" description="Four AI services for businesses: audit, customer communication, back-office automation, and training." skyWash>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="hero-label">Services</p>
      <h1>Everything is aimed at one thing: <em>lower costs, fewer wasted hours.</em></h1>
      <p>Four services, taken in order — or just the one you need. Each one ends with something working in your business, not a report that sits in a drawer.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- The four services -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <div class="service-rows">
        <div class="service-row">
          <span class="num">SERVICE 01</span>
          <h3>AI Opportunity Audit</h3>
          <p>A focused review of how your business runs day to day. We shadow the routine work — calls, inbox, scheduling, paperwork — and produce a short, ranked plan.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Workflow walkthrough with you and your team</li>
            <li>Ranked list: what to automate, what to leave alone</li>
            <li>Tool costs laid out before you commit to anything</li>
            <li>Clear next step, whether or not you hire us further</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="service-row">
          <span class="num">SERVICE 02</span>
          <h3>Customer Communication</h3>
          <p>The questions your customers ask every day — hours, availability, prices, directions, policies — answered accurately and instantly, with a human always one step away.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Website &amp; inbox assistant trained on your real answers</li>
            <li>Missed-call and after-hours response</li>
            <li>Review requests and follow-ups that actually go out</li>
            <li>Escalation rules so nothing important gets auto-answered wrong</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-400);">Restaurants · Salons &amp; clinics · Retail · Home services</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-row">
          <span class="num">SERVICE 03</span>
          <h3>Back-Office Automation</h3>
          <p>The invisible work: invoices, data entry, scheduling, reminders, document drafting, inventory lists. We connect the tools you already use so information stops being typed twice.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Scheduling, reminders &amp; no-show reduction</li>
            <li>Invoice, quote &amp; document drafting</li>
            <li>Data entry between your existing systems</li>
            <li>Weekly summaries of sales, bookings &amp; tasks</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-400);">Offices · Contractors · Clinics · Agencies</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-row">
          <span class="num">SERVICE 04</span>
          <h3>Training &amp; Ongoing Support</h3>
          <p>Tools only save money when people actually use them. We train your team in short, practical sessions and stay available as the tools — and your business — change.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Hands-on training for owners and staff</li>
            <li>Simple written guides in plain English</li>
            <li>Check-ins to tune, fix, and simplify</li>
            <li>Help evaluating the next tool before you pay for it</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- Trio -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">WHAT WE WORK WITH</span>
          <h3>What we work with</h3>
          <p>Your existing email, calendar, website, point-of-sale, booking, and office software first. New tools are only added when they clearly beat what you already pay for — and you own every account.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">WHAT WE DON&rsquo;T DO</span>
          <h3>What we don&rsquo;t do</h3>
          <p>No custom AI models you don&rsquo;t need, no replacing your staff, no long contracts to justify a setup, and no automating anything customer-facing without escalation rules and testing first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">HOW COSTS ARE SHOWN</span>
          <h3>How costs are shown</h3>
          <p>Tool subscriptions and our fees are itemized separately, in writing, before work starts. You see the expected payoff from the audit before you commit to a build — if the math doesn&rsquo;t work, we say so.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- FAQs -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Straight answers</h2>
        <p>Questions every owner asks us</p>
      </div>
      <details class="faq">
        <summary>I&rsquo;m not technical. Is this going to be over my head?</summary>
        <p>No — that&rsquo;s the point of hiring us. We handle selection, setup, and configuration. What you get is a short training session and a plain-English guide. If a tool needs constant technical care, it&rsquo;s the wrong tool for a local business and we won&rsquo;t install it.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq">
        <summary>Will AI replace my staff?</summary>
        <p>That&rsquo;s not the goal, and it&rsquo;s not what we set up. The wins for local businesses are in the repetitive edges — answering the same ten questions, re-typing the same information, chasing the same reminders — so your people spend their hours on customers, craft, and work that actually needs a person.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq">
        <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
        <p>It depends on the size of the setup, and we&rsquo;ll lay out tool costs and our costs separately, in writing, before any work starts. The audit comes first specifically so you can see the expected payoff before committing to a build. If the math doesn&rsquo;t work, we&rsquo;ll tell you.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq">
        <summary>Is my business data safe?</summary>
        <p>We only recommend tools with clear data controls, we configure the privacy settings as part of every setup, and your customer information stays in your accounts — never ours. We&rsquo;ll walk you through exactly what goes where before anything is switched on.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq">
        <summary>What if it doesn&rsquo;t work for us?</summary>
        <p>Then we simplify or remove it. We build in small steps — one workflow working and paying off before the next begins — precisely so you&rsquo;re never stuck with a big system you regret.</p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150); padding-bottom: 118px;">
      <div class="contact-cta-box">
        <h2>Start with the audit.</h2>
        <p>See the expected payoff before you commit to a build.</p>
        <div class="contact-cta-actions">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact" style="padding: 12px 24px; font-size: 14.5px;">Contact Us →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

</Layout>
